---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CategoryHub from '../../components/CategoryHub.astro';
import AffiliateDisclosure from '../../components/AffiliateDisclosure.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Donor CRM software for nonprofits"
  description="Bloomerang, Little Green Light, DonorDock, Neon and more: donor CRMs compared by real price, database size, and the shop they fit."
  section="donor-crm">
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Donor CRM' }]} />
    <section class="prose" style="margin-top: 1.2rem;">
      <p class="kicker">Category guide</p>
      <h1>Donor CRM software</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The donor CRM is your database of record: every donor, gift, and
        relationship in one place. Credible options start at $39-$45 a month and
        most price by the size of your database, not your team.
      </p>

      <h2>How to choose</h2>
      <p>
        Pick by who will run it. A solo fundraiser wants approachable and cheap:
        <a href="/go/littlegreenlight" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener">Little Green Light</a>
        ($45/mo) for value, or
        <a href="/go/donordock" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener">DonorDock</a>
        (from ~$98/mo, 90-day guarantee) if you want the software to drive your
        daily follow-up. A team of three to eight wants adoption and retention
        analytics, which is
        <a href="/go/bloomerang" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener">Bloomerang's</a>
        home turf (from $79/mo). Membership and event-heavy organizations should
        demo <a href="/go/neoncrm" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener">Neon CRM</a>
        before buying separate tools.
      </p>
      <p>
        Two habits save the most grief. Clean your list before you migrate,
        since most CRMs bill by record count. And run a test import during any
        trial to confirm gift history and soft credits arrive intact; a demo
        with your own data beats a demo with sample data.
      </p>
    </section>

    <CategoryHub category="donor-crm" />

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The first real CRM enters at <a href="/stacks/250k-1m/">$250k-$1M</a>;
        see the upgrades at <a href="/stacks/1m-5m/">$1M-$5M</a> and
        <a href="/stacks/5m-plus/">$5M+</a>.
      </p>
      <AffiliateDisclosure />
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
